00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:21,000
Miss Americana (also known as Taylor Swift: Miss Americana) is a 2020 American documentary film that follows
the singer-songwriter Taylor Swift and her life over the course of several years of her career.

10
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
It was directed by Lana Wilson, produced by Tremolo Productions, and
released to Netflix and select theaters on January 31, 2020.

11
00:46:45,000 --> 00:46:51,000
The film is titled after "Miss Americana & the
Heartbreak Prince", a 2019 song by Swift.

12
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
The film has been described as an unvarnished and emotionally revealing look at Swift, during a metamorphic phase in her life, as she learns to accept her role as not only a singer-songwriter and entertainer, but as an influential woman "harnessing the full power of her
voice." It is set in the time period spanning from Swift's Reputation Stadium Tour (2018) to the release roll-out of her seventh studio album, Lover (2019), dotted with flashback video clips portraying several undisclosed events of her life and career.

13
00:55:15,000 --> 00:55:21,000
Premiering at the opening night of 2020 Sundance Film Festival on January 23, 2020, Miss
Americana was praised for its emotion, intimacy, and vulnerable topics.

14
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
Reviews complimented Swift's honesty and personality.

15
01:03:45,000 --> 01:03:51,000
Accompanying the film's release, "Only the Young", a song by Swift featured
in the end credits, was released as a promotional single.

16
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Miss Americana was selected by the National Board of Review as
one of the five best documentaries of 2020.

17
01:12:15,000 --> 01:12:21,000
Publications have named it amongst the best Netflix films and biographical
documentaries and regard it a pivotal moment for Swift's career.

18
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
The film explores themes of politics, pop star, pop
culture, behind the scenes, pop music.

19
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:51,000
The tone is emotional.
